# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_onboard_all_repos.py" "ALL-REPOS ONBOARDING GATE: PASS" "All-repositories install onboards every repo (the silent-install-for-orgs fix)" "All-repositories install onboards via the installation_repos fallback: GitHub OMITS the \`repositories\` array from the installation.created webhook when the install scope is 'All repositories' (repository_selection == 'all') -- the DEFAULT, most-common org install. The App's OWN offboarding already accounts for this (purge_account_working_set is account-WIDE precisely because that array is absent), but the ONBOARDING handler read ONLY payload['repositories'] and, finding it absent, cold-started ZERO repos: no graph ingested, no open-PR backfill, and no 'Veripsa is now watching' check -- an org grants code-read on its whole account and sees TOTAL SILENCE until each repo's next push to main. THE FIX (ingest._onboard_repos): when the payload names NO repos, ENUMERATE the installation's repos via gh.installation_repos and onboard those. Bounded TWO ways -- discovery paging stops at _ONBOARD_DISCOVER_CAP and only the first _ONBOARD_REPO_CAP are cold-started now, with the rest honestly DEFERRED. Guarded + fail-open: no installation_repos method or a transient list error onboards nothing. The same gate now locks lifecycle and replay boundaries discovered during exact-head review: a name-only backfill promotes only a matching current PR base.repo.id into its synthetic work event; its nested base/head repository ids preserve fork redaction; missing fork identity selects the redacted surface without disabling required-check or pause behavior; malformed draft values cannot soften a collision; repository ids are positive canonical ASCII integers; current base SHA, head ref, draft state, changed-file count, and bounded label names preserve live replay semantics; a repository add with no observed durable lifecycle authority never clones or onboards; and a current DB-observed add still onboards normally. WHAT THIS GATE PROVES (PURE + OFFLINE): (1-10) the original all-repositories fallback, bounds, failure, and selected-install behavior; (11) missing account-onboarding authority fails closed; (12) stable identity write failure escapes; (13) matching base repository id is preserved while a foreign coordinate id is rejected; (14) missing durable repository lifecycle authority yields zero clones; (15) observed current lifecycle authority preserves the positive onboarding path; (16) backfill remains fork-aware and preserves bounded freshness, draft, changed-file, and ACK metadata; (17) unknown fork identity is redacted while merge gating remains active and malformed draft is strict; (18) invalid or Unicode-digit repository ids cannot become lifecycle authority. Content-free throughout (repo full_names, ids, refs, SHAs, label names, and counts only, never bodies); advisory." 24
